{"type":"standard","title":"Brian Babin","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Brian Babin</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q16979824","titles":{"canonical":"Brian_Babin","normalized":"Brian Babin","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Brian Babin</span></span>"},"pageid":42119569,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Brian_Babin_115th_Congress.jpg/330px-Brian_Babin_115th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":496},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/Brian_Babin_115th_Congress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2662,"height":4000},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1353875924","tid":"208477be-4e53-11f1-a76a-0c604ffd90b9","timestamp":"2026-05-12T22:37:16Z","description":"American dentist and politician (born 1948)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brian_Babin","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brian_Babin?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brian_Babin?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Brian_Babin"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brian_Babin","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Brian_Babin","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brian_Babin?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Brian_Babin"}},"extract":"Brian Philip Babin is an American dentist, politician and member of the Republican Party who has served as the U.S. representative from Texas's 36th congressional district since 2015. The district includes much of southeastern Houston, some of its eastern suburbs, and some more exurban and rural areas to the east.","extract_html":"<p><b>Brian Philip Babin</b> is an American dentist, politician and member of the Republican Party who has served as the U.S. representative from Texas's 36th congressional district since 2015. The district includes much of southeastern Houston, some of its eastern suburbs, and some more exurban and rural areas to the east.</p>"}